    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required assigning `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n`membershipNumber` is a purely **derived, read-only** value \u2014 it comes entirely from `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, both of which are already populated on every persisted owner. This is exactly the pattern the project already uses for the derived `displayName` and `initials` fields, which are computed in the MapStruct mapper rather than stored. So I followed that established convention instead of adding a persisted column or a new OfficeFloor step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping expression to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   `%02d` on `year % 100` correctly yields the zero-padded last two digits (e.g. 2026 \u2192 `26`, 2005 \u2192 `05`), matching the test's `registrationDate.substring(2,4)` expectation.\n\nBecause both the Spring and OfficeFloor response paths produce `OwnerDto` through this mapper, both arms now return `membershipNumber` automatically \u2014 no new function class or POST-flow step was needed.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
